    "answer": {
      "short": "The $60^\\circ$ sector, by around $0.13\\text{ cm}^2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}r_{60^\\circ}&=\\frac{26}{2}=13\\text{ cm}\\\\A_{45^\\circ}&=\\frac{45}{360}\\times\\pi(15)^2\\\\A_{45^\\circ}&=\\frac{225\\pi}{8}\\text{ cm}^2\\\\A_{60^\\circ}&=\\frac{60}{360}\\times\\pi(13)^2\\\\A_{60^\\circ}&=\\frac{169\\pi}{6}\\text{ cm}^2\\\\A_{60^\\circ}-A_{45^\\circ}&=\\frac{169\\pi}{6}-\\frac{225\\pi}{8}\\\\A_{60^\\circ}-A_{45^\\circ}&=\\frac{\\pi}{24}\\text{ cm}^2\\\\A_{60^\\circ}-A_{45^\\circ}&\\approx0.13\\text{ cm}^2\\end{align*}$$\nThe $60^\\circ$ sector gives the bigger area, by $0.13\\text{ cm}^2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
